TV client UX track (FR-1/2/3/7) - library screens.

Root causes found:
1. movie_detail_screen.dart:223 had autofocus:true on the Back FocusableAction, so
   entering a movie put the first Select on Back (FR-7).
2. MediaHero pinned the title at fontSize 44 with maxLines 2 + ellipsis while
   series_detail_screen.dart:444 puts it in an Expanded(flex:4) pane of the two-pane
   Row (~300 px of a 1119 px content area, after the 150 px poster and padding).
   'How I Met Your Mother' needs ~484 px at 44 px, i.e. a third line, so it clipped (FR-2).
3. PosterCard used BoxFit.cover into a 165x~240 portrait frame; most library items only
   have landscape backdrops, which cover cropped to a middle strip (FR-1).
4. Series detail left every non-Down hop to Flutter's directional (geometric) policy, and
   EpisodeList had onExitUp defined but never wired by the host, so Up from the season
   chips fell through to geometry (FR-3).

Deliberate non-changes (contracts that must not regress):
- Down from the CTA still enters the episode list (owner fix 2026-11-07).
- Left from the content area still reaches the rail (pinned by library_dpad_test.dart);
  an onExitLeft interception was implemented and then reverted for this reason.

